
%9Syntax:%9

WEBJOURNAL%|

%9Description:%9

    Shows the state of the window journal: whether it is enabled, the
    directory, and the number of entries written, file rotations and
    errors (with the last error). The counters start when the script is
    loaded. Arguments are ignored; the journal is turned on and off with
    /SET webjournal. A command of the webjournal.pl script.

    The script writes to disk everything visible in erssi windows, so that
    the web client can fill in gaps after a restart:
      <dir>/<tag>/<channel|nick>.jsonl   channel and query messages (JSON
                                         entries: time, kind, nick, text),
                                         plus client and script messages
                                         shown in those windows,
      <dir>/<tag>/%%status.jsonl          the status window of network <tag>,
      <dir>/%%windows/<name>.jsonl        other named windows (Notices,
                                         Mentions...).

    Quits and joins hidden by a netsplit summary (hide_netsplit_quits)
    are written too, so the web client knows who left and came back.

    Names are stored in lower case, characters outside [a-z0-9#&+!._-] as
    %%XX. Messages ignored with /IGNORE are not written. A file larger than
    webjournal_max_kb is renamed to <file>.1 (the previous .1 is removed).
    Files have mode 0600, directories 0700.

%9Settings:%9

    webjournal = ON
        Write the journal.
    webjournal_dir = ~/.erssi/journal
        The journal directory.
    webjournal_max_kb = 2048
        File size that triggers rotation (0 or less = 2048).

%9Examples:%9

    /WEBJOURNAL
    /SET webjournal OFF

%9See also:%9 LOG, SET

